              "Since Beijing must also know these facts of life, the decision to take such extreme steps speaks less to Chinese leverage than to Beijing’s difficult position in this trade dispute. China was always at a disadvantage to the United States in this matter. Some 25% of China’s all-important export effort goes to the United States, fully 5% of its economy.  That is a considerable dependence.  In contrast, less than 10% of America’s relatively less important export sector goes to China, less than 2% of the U.S. economy",
